From dbe63e43847b7a4b453d70f05649f89c2ee52f1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iceland-dev <dev@iceland.local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 04:28:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] virt: gunyah: adapt to mainline 7.2

Logic is unchanged; the edits are API-form adaptations, each listed in
Documentation/virt/gunyah/port_adaptations.md:

 - rsc_mgr.h: <linux/android_kabi.h> only exists on Android GKI trees.
   Include it when present, otherwise define
   ANDROID_KABI_ENUMERATOR_IGNORE() as a no-op (it is an ABI-tool hint).
 - gunyah_vcpu.c, vm_mgr.c: the Android restricted vendor hooks
   (trace_android_rvh_gh_*) have no infrastructure on mainline.  Route
   them through gunyah_vendor_hooks.h, which forwards to
   <trace/hooks/gunyah.h> under CONFIG_ANDROID_VENDOR_HOOKS and provides
   empty inline stubs otherwise.
 - vm_mgr.h: set_direct_map_{invalid,default}_noflush() are not exported
   to modules on mainline arm64.  Factor both loops into
   gunyah_folio_set_direct_map(), compiled out under MODULE.  Lent memory
   stays protected by the hypervisor's stage-2 unmap.
 - rsc_mgr.c: of_node_to_fwnode() was renamed to of_fwnode_handle().

Builds with zero warnings (clang/LLVM=1).  Verified on OnePlus Pad 4
(SM8850): all ten modules load, the core driver reports "Running under
Gunyah hypervisor 51/v1", /dev/gunyah and the gh_rm_core auxiliary
device appear, and the Qualcomm platform hooks register.
